  "id": "pierre-robin-sequence",
  "term": "Pierre Robin sequence",
  "definition": "Pierre Robin sequence is a rare congenital condition marked by a small lower jaw, backward displacement of the tongue, and blockage of the airway. Because of these features, babies with this condition can be especially difficult to manage when breathing support or intubation is needed.",
